NtCreateUserProcess does not exist in Windows XP. It was introduced later as the native, low-level process creation API in Windows Vista (Windows NT kernel version 6.0). [https://community.osr.com/t/ssdt-hooks-for-process-creation-xp-vista-w7/39080, https://forum.madshi.net/viewtopic.php?t=4941]
In Windows XP (NT kernel version 5.1), the kernel used older, legacy process creation APIs. we would typically work with these alternatives: [https://forum.madshi.net/viewtopic.php?t=4941, https://www.evilsocket.net/2014/02/11/On-Windows-syscall-mechanism-and-syscall-numbers-extraction-methods/]
• NtCreateProcess / NtCreateProcessEx: The foundational system calls used in Windows XP to establish the core process structures in the kernel.
• RtlCreateUserProcess: The documented, user-mode NTDLL function that wraps the process setup logic in XP. [https://forum.madshi.net/viewtopic.php?t=4941, https://stackoverflow.com/questions/15424900/do-all-user-mode-processes-started-in-windows-go-through-createprocess, https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/rtlcreateuserprocess-dana-behling-u0yoc]

