☐ @low Application Hives (\REGISTRY\A): Modern Windows uses this for UWP/AppX isolated hives. my code will return false for these because they don't start with MACHINE or USER. Sandboxie handles these with some highly specific hooks, but for a standard Win32 desktop application sandbox, it is perfectly safe to let them fail to resolve or pass through, as Win32 desktop apps generally do not have the permissions or context to write to \REGISTRY\A anyway.

